[en.EVENT_JOKES_21]
Changeling Service

[en.EVENT_JOKES_21_desc]
As the trade in Ponyville opened up, the number of Changelings in Ponyville increased, and a new service industry was developed — Changeling Service.
One day, the rich merchant Filty Rich saw a Changeling Service store, where the Changelings in the store could transform into any pony, even a well-known pony.
Filty Rich was a little curious, so he walked into the store, and the clerk asked him what service he needed. He hesitated a bit, but still tried it out, asking the clerk to transform into the singer Coloratura. Filty Rich had a pleasant evening and left satisfied.
A few days later, Filty Rich couldn’t help but come to the Changeling Service store again. This time he asked the clerk to transform into Duchess Trixie. This experience also made him very satisfied.
A few days later, Filty Rich came to the Changeling Service store again, asking the clerk to transform into his wife, Spoiled Rich, but asked the clerk to be gentler. Filty Rich had another pleasant evening.
The fourth time, Filty Rich came to the Changeling Service store again, this time he wanted a little excitement, asking to spend the night with a bugbear.
A week later, Filty Rich came to the Changeling Service store for the fifth time. During the chat, he praised the clerk’s service, but the clerk was very surprised:
"Last week, due to a bugbear disaster in this neighborhood, we closed the store temporarily!"

[en.EVENT_JOKES_21_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_JOKES_21_o1]
Random Joke

[en.EVENT_JOKES_21_o2]
Next Joke

[en.EVENT_JOKES_21_o3]
Prev Joke

[en.EVENT_JOKES_22]
Necromancy

[en.EVENT_JOKES_22_desc]
In Las Pegasus, fraud has become a normal way of making profits, and many inexplicable shops and services are taking advantage of this. One day, a pony walked into a necromancy shop in Las Pegasus, and the shopkeeper told him that he could talk to his ancestors as long as he paid a certain fee.
Although the pony was very sure that this was a scam, he was still ready to try it out because he remembered that his grandfather had left him a huge inheritance, but he didn’t know where it was. He asked the shopkeeper who had already communicated with the dead, "Grandpa, did you leave anything for me?"
The shopkeeper did not reply in the voice of the grandfather. He just told the pony that he had to pay more for such questions. The pony was a little unhappy, but he added money to continue asking. The shopkeeper possessed again, but still did not answer the question. No matter how the pony asked, the shopkeeper did not answer. He began to suspect that the shopkeeper was just trying to get money, so he accused the shopkeeper of being a fraud and decided to leave.
But the shopkeeper stopped him, apologized, and explained that it was indeed his grandfather who did not speak, not himself refusing to deliver the answer. To prove his sincere apology, he returned all the money to the pony.
The pony felt that he had wronged the shopkeeper, so he returned to the shop the next day to try again, only to find that the necromancy shop had closed.
After inquiring around, the pony learned that after closing yesterday, the shopkeeper went out with a shovel and has not returned yet.

[en.EVENT_JOKES_22_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_JOKES_22_o1]
Random Joke

[en.EVENT_JOKES_22_o2]
Next Joke

[en.EVENT_JOKES_22_o3]
